# _paperDemo/.gitignore — this project's own rules, applied on top of the repo root's.

# The Co-host archive is a deliberate part of the record, not a regenerable output: CLAIMS v9
# archived the Fe-Co/Fe-Co-B models and _archive/cofe/ holds the frozen values, the evidence
# extract and the archived structures. The repo root ignores `_archive/` wholesale, and also
# `*.csv` / `*.xsf` as regenerable artifacts, so both are re-enabled here for that one directory.
# Verified with `git check-ignore -v`; see _archive/cofe/README.md.
!_archive/
!_archive/cofe/
!_archive/cofe/**.csv
!_archive/cofe/**.xsf
!_archive/cofe/**.md
!_archive/cofe/**.json
!_archive/cofe/**.py
!_archive/cofe/**.png

# LaTeX build artifacts (E2 port). The sources (paper.tex, SI.tex, latex/*.tex) and the compiled
# PDFs are tracked, as with the other generated-but-record artifacts (figures/*.png, analysis/*.csv);
# only the intermediate files are ignored.
*.aux
*.blg
*.bbl
*.out
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex.gz
*.log

# === data/ — the AGOX result databases, tracked on the scientist's instruction (2026-09-18) ======
# Reversal of the previous rule ("the data tree is not part of paper commits"). The repo root
# ignores *.db / *.out / *.txt / *.xsf / *.csv as regenerable artifacts; the set of *root* ignores
# is harmless, but the structure databases are NOT regenerable - they are the search output every
# reported number comes from - so they are re-enabled here, together with the run code that
# produced them.
!data/
!data/**/
!data/**/*.db
!data/**/*.py
!data/**/*.sh

# Still ignored (ask if wanted): *.xsf, *.traj, *.csv, *.txt and *.out under data/. The GPAW
# console/text dumps alone are 36 638 files / ~3.9 GB of regenerable output and carry no number
# that analysis/*.csv + the .db do not already carry.

# Scratch/bookkeeping trees inside the runs stay excluded, in git as in the analysis.
data/**/trash/
data/**/_trash/

# These run-directory script snapshots carry a copy of their OWN git repository (a nested .git
# directory). Git cannot descend into a directory that contains one -- it would record a bare
# gitlink instead of the files -- so they are excluded until those nested .git copies are removed.
# The databases and the run configuration (main.py) of these same runs ARE tracked; only the
# helper-script copies are held back.
data/dos_femgo_flatngs/scripts/
data/febmgo/scripts/
data/febmgo_v2/scripts/
data/mgofe/scripts/
